description:
The paper validates the VCell hybrid method (finite volume PDE plus Smoldyn, fixed-step
operator splitting) on calcium sparks, with stochastic two-state channels coupled to a
diffusing Ca2+ field:
- Test 1 (separable) against an analytic expectation;
- Test 2 (fast diffusion) against a non-spatial Gibson-Bruck SSA;
- Tests 3-5 against direct functional Fokker-Planck solutions;
- Test 6, stochastically gated binding in 3D, and Test 7, cell polarization.
Each study here re-runs a test through both solvers and regenerates the matching figure
with both results overlaid. The native solver is driven headlessly through pyvcell /
libvcell / pyvcell-fvsolver (Phase 3).
